<Base current="about" title="Our story | The Common Squamish" description="The Common brings people together around good work, shared space, and community in downtown Squamish.">
  <header class="page-hd"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow on-dark">Our story</span><h1>Work together.<br />Grow together.</h1><p>How a coworking space on Cleveland Avenue became part of the Squamish community.</p></div></header>
  <section class="section light"><div class="wrap split"><div><span class="kicker">Since 2017</span><h2>Why Peter opened The Common.</h2><p>Peter Buchholz opened The Common in 2017. He wanted independent workers to have a good place to work and a chance to get to know the people around them.</p><p>Today, remote workers, small teams, and local businesses share the space on Cleveland Avenue. You can come in for an hour or make it part of your regular week.</p><a class="inline-link" href="/community/">Read about the community</a></div><img class="photo" src="/img/approved/shared-table.jpg" alt="People working together around a table at The Common" loading="lazy" /></div></section>
  <section class="section warm"><div class="wrap split"><img class="photo" src="/img/approved/kitchen.jpg" alt="Kitchen and lounge at The Common" loading="lazy" /><div><span class="kicker">A day here</span><h2>What it's like to work here.</h2><p>Desks have monitors. You can book a room for a private meeting, use the phone booth for a short call, make lunch in the kitchen, or take a break in the courtyard.</p><p>If you want to try the space, book a desk for an hour or a day. Monthly plans are available if you come in more often.</p><a class="inline-link" href="/day-pass/">Book a desk</a></div></div></section>
  <section class="section light"><div class="wrap statement"><span class="kicker">The Common in Squamish</span><h2>There's a history behind the name.</h2><p>The Common took inspiration from the idea of social capital: people sharing time, skills, and introductions. Over the years, members have gathered for lunches and socials, and the space has supported local groups and events.</p><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/community/">Read the community story</a></div></section>
</Base>
<style>.split h2,.statement h2{font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3.4rem);letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:.8rem 0 1.3rem}.split p,.statement p{font-size:1.08rem;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:1.2rem}.split .photo{aspect-ratio:1.2}.statement{max-width:850px;text-align:center}.statement p{max-width:720px;margin:0 auto 1.8rem}</style>
